+# Decision 0001: free shipping is judged on goods after every discount
+
+Date: 2026-11-17
+
+## Context
+Support reported a customer charged €4.90 shipping on "goods of exactly €50.00". The code already
+ships free at goods >= €50.00 (`FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS`), and the README defines goods as the amount
+after every discount and before VAT. The report could not be reproduced, and no order number was
+available. The likeliest cause is €50.00 before a coupon or volume discount.
+
+## Decision
+Keep the code and the README rule as they are. Add boundary tests (net exactly €50.00 ships free,
+net below it pays the band cost). If a Goods line of €50.00 or more with shipping charged turns up
+on a real receipt, treat it as a new bug. If the customer's €50.00 was pre-discount, the site
+wording should change, not the rule.
+
+## Consequences
+No behaviour change. The site's promise should say "after discounts".
